# Line-ending policy.
#
# This repo is developed on Windows, but the Makefile and the shell scripts under
# scripts/ are run by bash — locally, and in CI. A CRLF shell script fails with the
# notoriously opaque:
#
#     /usr/bin/env: 'bash\r': No such file or directory
#
# git's core.autocrlf=true (the Windows default) rewrites these files on checkout,
# so the policy has to be pinned per file type rather than left to local config.

# Default: let git decide for text, but never touch anything it detects as binary.
* text=auto

# Must be LF — executed by bash, or read by a tool that does not tolerate CR.
*.sh            text eol=lf
*.bash          text eol=lf
*.py            text eol=lf
*.env.example   text eol=lf
Makefile        text eol=lf

# Config formats that get parsed on Linux hosts.
*.yaml          text eol=lf
*.yml           text eol=lf
*.toml          text eol=lf

# Binary — never convert.
*.png           binary
*.jpg           binary
*.gif           binary
*.ico           binary
*.pdf           binary
*.wasm          binary
